      "details": "The function allocates payload with devm_kmalloc, copies caller data into it, passes it to the synchronous flash writer, and reaches common cleanup without a devm_kfree for payload. The only caller cleanup free uses access.managed_allocation. The stock Ghidra pseudocode and exact stock assembly show the same allocation, call, and cleanup: devm_kmalloc at 0x213bc; payload is passed in x3 to syna_tcm_write_flash at 0x21408; the only devm_kfree call at 0x21454 uses the separate access allocation held in x19/local_b0. The callee reads/copies the input pointer and does not free it. Consequently, each invocation that gets as far as allocating payload retains rounded_length bytes under devres until managed-device teardown; repeated invocations can accumulate retained memory before detach. This is not a permanent leak after device teardown.",
